# {{name}} — Claude Code Guidelines

This project uses spec-driven development with the Qontinui UI Bridge and a
compiled design language.

## Specs and states

- Specs live in `specs/pages/<id>/`.
- Author states with `<State>` and transitions with `<TransitionTo>` from
  `@qontinui/ui-bridge`; the ui-bridge-auto Vite plugin (`uiBridgeIRPlugin`
  in `vite.config.ts`) derives the state-machine IR at build time into
  `src/state-machine.derived.json`.
- Keep every page reachable through declared transitions so automated spec
  checks can walk the whole app.

## Design

The visual system is a source file, `design/language.dtcg.json`, that
`design-kit` compiles into `src/design/` (CSS custom properties, typed
constants, an exclusive Tailwind theme, a style guide, budgets and thresholds).
The compiled files are committed; never edit them by hand.

Resolve, then author. When a page needs a colour, a spacing step, a type size,
a radius or an elevation, resolve it from the declared visual system (a
`--dk-*` token or a Tailwind class the theme generates) and never mint a
literal: no `bg-[#f00]`, no `p-[13px]`, no hex, `rgb()` or `px` value in a
`.tsx` file. Compose screens from the kit components below before writing a
new one. A colour or a typeface that `design/language.dtcg.json` marks
`undeclared` stays undeclared: say so, and do not pick one. The browser's own
system colours and font render in its place until the owner declares them.
Structural values (a spacing step, a radius) may be authored in the source file
with a recorded `authored(<notification_ref>)` source; hue, typeface and
illustration style never may.

Every interactive element needs all its states (default, hover, focus-visible,
active, disabled, loading, error, selected, where they apply) and every list
screen needs its empty, loading, error and filtered-empty states; the kit's
`RecordListPage` makes the four screen states required props.

`design-kit` verbs (run with `npx design-kit <verb>`):

- `compile` / `compile --check` — rebuild `src/design/` from the source / fail on drift.
- `status` — each group's state and the next undeclared group.
- `specimen` / `specimen --check` — write / verify `specimen.html`, every component in every state.
- `check-states specimen.html` — measure each state's style change through the
  UI Bridge exec door (needs Playwright's Chromium); `focus-visible` reports
  `unknown(focus-visible-not-emulated)`.
- `lint-classes src` — find arbitrary-value classes and inline literal colours or lengths.
- `index` / `index --check` — regenerate / verify the component index below.
- `diff --base <ref>` — mark budgets and thresholds that moved toward permissive.

After changing the source, run `npm run design:compile`. `npm run build` runs
every check above and fails on drift.

